// ADR 0047 — a mutable `var` shared with a spawn is conservatively
// flagged (name-based linter, no happens-before analysis yet).
//
// Now:   REJECTED by the conservative pass in
//        `src/semantics/race/mod.rs`. Matches
//        `test_var_sharing_with_spawn_is_conservatively_flagged`.
// After: This specific case may remain rejected under ADR 0047's
//        real memory model — the spawn has no synchronization with
//        `print(x)` in main, so a data race is genuinely possible.
//        The point of ADR 0047 is to accept cases like
//        `spawn { x := 1 }; join; print(x)` where HB is provable.
proc main
    var x := 42
    spawn
        print(x)
    print(x)